  "calibration": {
    "e_d_half_metres": 0.175,
    "e_d_rationale": "The Youden-optimal separation between the two measured neighbour-step distributions in scene_geometry_scale: the depth step at which 'same surface' stops explaining the difference and 'different object' starts. The separation curve is FLAT over [0.10, 0.35] m, so the third digit carries no weight and the value must not be re-tuned to move a result.",
    "e_n_half": 0.1339745962155613,
    "e_n_half_degrees": 30.0,
    "e_n_rationale": "1 - cos(30 deg). A 30-degree orientation change is a change of facet; correctly-tracked normals sit far below it (see error_distributions), and a 90-degree cube edge lands at 2^-7.5 = 0.006, i.e. effectively zero. NOT LOAD-BEARING ON THIS SCENE: the geometry is axis-aligned boxes and a ground plane, so the normal separation is near-binary and its Youden index is flat across 10-60 degrees (see scene_geometry_scale.normal_separation). Curved geometry would make this term discriminative and would need the calibration re-run.",
