      "item": "\u00a74's e_D is undefined on background, on BOTH sides of the subtraction",
      "detail": "depth carries +inf for background, so |D_t - W(D_{t-1})| is inf-inf = NaN when either operand is sky. Zeroing only the current-frame side leaves the 'was sky, is surface now' disocclusion undefined. A fifth hard zero on the warped source's background coverage was added; it is not in \u00a74's three lines.",
      "action": "needs a Decision Log entry \u2014 NOT written by this run"
    },
    {
      "item": "e_N is not renormalised after warping",
      "detail": "\u00a74's form taken literally. Bilinear interpolation across a silhouette shortens the warped normal and so raises e_N there, conflating interpolation shortening with genuine orientation mismatch. Both distributions are measured above; the difference is confined to the top percentile.",
      "action": "needs a Decision Log entry \u2014 NOT written by this run"
    },
